From 93b04bdb0a513fd6776892be5a4451b53c7df4e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 23:22:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] docs: describe Chimera runtime integration

Document the implemented DPMS, hardware cursor, and DDC/CI paths while keeping live-dock validation and recovery work clearly separated from offline build and protocol coverage.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
---
 README.md         |  8 ++++----
 chimera/README.md | 13 ++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index df86466..03d0d40 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -148,10 +148,10 @@ and clean teardown on dock unplug. See `docs/` for the design notes and the
 kernel-tree patch set.
 
 **Chimera:** the production service connects Revdi frames to the Vino control,
-mode, codec, and USB paths. Its optimized build and offline tests pass. The
-cleanup revision has not been exercised against hardware, so live parity,
-replug, cursor, DDC/CI, and recovery behavior still require the hardware test
-matrix described in the companion Vino repository.
+mode, codec, USB, DPMS, cursor, DDC/CI, dynamic-topology, and session-recovery
+paths. Its optimized build and offline tests pass. The cleanup revision has not
+been exercised against hardware, so live parity remains a validation claim
+until the hardware test matrix in the companion Vino repository is complete.
 
 ## License
 
diff --git a/chimera/README.md b/chimera/README.md
index 5e825b5..b426e17 100644
--- a/chimera/README.md
+++ b/chimera/README.md
@@ -32,7 +32,11 @@ The daemon:
 5. applies the compositor-selected captured mode profile;
 6. sends the video-arm prefix and training carrier; and
 7. encodes coherent Revdi updates with Vino's kernel codec and submits them to the matching USB
-   endpoint.
+   endpoint;
+8. forwards DPMS and hardware-cursor state; and
+9. completes Revdi DDC/CI writes and reads through Vino's encrypted monitor-control tunnel;
+10. debounces monitor removal and recreates Revdi outputs after reattachment; and
+11. rebuilds the owned dock session after transport failure.
 
 No module loading, kernel installation, service management, or reboot is performed by Chimera.
 
@@ -47,8 +51,11 @@ cargo test -p vino-chimera --all-features
 ```
 
 The oracle checks byte-exact control sealing, message builders, codec records, mode profiles, video
-arm construction, Revdi pixel conversion, and strip-grid padding. Hardware-dependent operations
-are deliberately excluded from the automated suite.
+arm construction, DDC/CI reply bounds, Revdi pixel conversion, cursor repacking, and strip-grid
+padding. Hardware-dependent operations are deliberately excluded from the automated suite.
+
+The DPMS, cursor, DDC/CI, topology, and session-recovery paths are implemented, but the cleanup
+revision has not been run against a live dock. They remain part of the hardware validation matrix.
 
 ## Source synchronization
 
